msgid "How this workspace works"
msgstr "How this workspace works"

msgid ""
"Six views. A map, a chart and a table show data, and three selectors set "
"what they show. They are linked through channels. This tour follows one "
"channel from start to end."
msgstr ""
"Six views. A map, a chart and a table show data, and three selectors set "
"what they show. They are linked through channels. This tour follows one "
"channel from start to end."

msgid "View headers"
msgstr "View headers"

msgid ""
"Every view has a header, with its name, its channels, and buttons to "
"maximize or close it. The demo starts without them, for a first look. The "
"Workspace tab shows them again."
msgstr ""
"Every view has a header, with its name, its channels, and buttons to "
"maximize or close it. The demo starts without them, for a first look. The "
"Workspace tab shows them again."

msgid "Views come from here"
msgstr "Views come from here"

msgid ""
"Up to 4 charts, maps or tables, and selectors and notes. Click a tile, or "
"drag it where you want it. Every view also gets a settings tab here."
msgstr ""
"Up to 4 charts, maps or tables, and selectors and notes. Click a tile, or "
"drag it where you want it. Every view also gets a settings tab here."

msgid "A channel"
msgstr "A channel"

msgid ""
"A channel carries one value of one dimension to every view in it. This "
"selector sets the org unit of channel {{channel}}, named by its letter and "
"color."
msgstr ""
"A channel carries one value of one dimension to every view in it. This "
"selector sets the org unit of channel {{channel}}, named by its letter and "
"color."

msgid "Who's in it"
msgstr "Who's in it"

msgid ""
"Each view's badges name its channels. The map's {{channel}} badge has an "
"arrow out, it sets the value when clicked, and an arrow in, it follows the "
"value. The chart and the table have the same badge."
msgstr ""
"Each view's badges name its channels. The map's {{channel}} badge has an "
"arrow out, it sets the value when clicked, and an arrow in, it follows the "
"value. The chart and the table have the same badge."

msgid "Where that is set"
msgstr "Where that is set"

msgid ""
"A view's settings tab has a Links section. For each dimension, it picks the "
"view's channel, whether the view sets the value by clicking, whether it "
"follows it, and how. Highlight only keeps the view's own periods or places, "
"and marks the value."
msgstr ""
"A view's settings tab has a Links section. For each dimension, it picks the "
"view's channel, whether the view sets the value by clicking, whether it "
"follows it, and how. Highlight only keeps the view's own periods or places, "
"and marks the value."

msgid "Set the value"
msgstr "Set the value"

msgid ""
"Click {{highest}} on the map, and the map sets the value of channel "
"{{channel}}. Or press Next, and the demo clicks it for you."
msgstr ""
"Click {{highest}} on the map, and the map sets the value of channel "
"{{channel}}. Or press Next, and the demo clicks it for you."

msgid "The value travels"
msgstr "The value travels"

msgid ""
"The tree selects {{highest}}, as it is in channel {{channel}} too. Pick "
"another org unit in it, and the map follows it in turn."
msgstr ""
"The tree selects {{highest}}, as it is in channel {{channel}} too. Pick "
"another org unit in it, and the map follows it in turn."

msgid "Followers rewrite their own item"
msgstr "Followers rewrite their own item"

msgid ""
"The chart follows channel {{channel}}. Its districts become {{highest}}'s "
"chiefdoms, as its saved item asks for the units below the one it shows. The "
"table narrows to them too. The map, which set the value, highlights it "
"rather than redrawing."
msgstr ""
"The chart follows channel {{channel}}. Its districts become {{highest}}'s "
"chiefdoms, as its saved item asks for the units below the one it shows. The "
"table narrows to them too. The map, which set the value, highlights it "
"rather than redrawing."

msgid "Another channel"
msgstr "Another channel"

msgid ""
"Channel {{channel}} carries a period the same way. Click a month's name "
"under the chart, and the map shows that month, while the table marks the "
"quarter holding it. A point carries its district too."
msgstr ""
"Channel {{channel}} carries a period the same way. Click a month's name "
"under the chart, and the map shows that month, while the table marks the "
"quarter holding it. A point carries its district too."

msgid "Play"
msgstr "Play"

msgid ""
"The timeline sets channel {{channel}} one month at a time. Press play, and "
"the map steps through the months, each step waiting until it has drawn. The "
"chart and the table follow with Highlight only, set in their Links. They "
"keep their own periods, and mark each month."
msgstr ""
"The timeline sets channel {{channel}} one month at a time. Press play, and "
"the map steps through the months, each step waiting until it has drawn. The "
"chart and the table follow with Highlight only, set in their Links. They "
"keep their own periods, and mark each month."

msgid "Start again"
msgstr "Start again"

msgid "Reset the demo brings this layout back at any time."
msgstr "Reset the demo brings this layout back at any time."

msgid "Over to you"
msgstr "Over to you"

msgid ""
"Add a view, link it in its settings, and click. The other tour, The story, "
"shows what the links reveal in this data."
msgstr ""
"Add a view, link it in its settings, and click. The other tour, The story, "
"shows what the links reveal in this data."

msgid "{{current}} of {{total}}"
msgstr "{{current}} of {{total}}"

msgid "Next"
msgstr "Next"

msgid "Back"
msgstr "Back"

msgid "Done"
msgstr "Done"

msgid "A question for Demoland"
msgstr "A question for Demoland"

msgid ""
"Malaria is endemic in Demoland, and it weighs far more in some places than "
"in others. Where, when, and why there? Three linked views answer it in a "
"few steps. The data is made up, but follows a pattern seen where malaria is "
"endemic."
msgstr ""
"Malaria is endemic in Demoland, and it weighs far more in some places than "
"in others. Where, when, and why there? Three linked views answer it in a "
"few steps. The data is made up, but follows a pattern seen where malaria is "
"endemic."

msgid "Where"
msgstr "Where"

msgid ""
"Confirmed malaria cases per 1,000 people a year. {{highest}} has "
"{{highestValue}}, {{ratio}} times {{lowest}} ({{lowestValue}}). A rate "
"compares places of different sizes, where case counts would mostly show "
"where people live."
msgstr ""
"Confirmed malaria cases per 1,000 people a year. {{highest}} has "
"{{highestValue}}, {{ratio}} times {{lowest}} ({{lowestValue}}). A rate "
"compares places of different sizes, where case counts would mostly show "
"where people live."

msgid "When"
msgstr "When"

msgid ""
"The same rate, month by month, a line per district. Malaria rises with the "
"rains from May, but {{highest}} has the highest rate every month. Its "
"problem is not the season."
msgstr ""
"The same rate, month by month, a line per district. Malaria rises with the "
"rains from May, but {{highest}} has the highest rate every month. Its "
"problem is not the season."

msgid "Ask the map"
msgstr "Ask the map"

msgid ""
"Click {{highest}} on the map, and every view answers for {{highest}}. Or "
"press Next, and the demo clicks it for you."
msgstr ""
"Click {{highest}} on the map, and every view answers for {{highest}}. Or "
"press Next, and the demo clicks it for you."

msgid "One click"
msgstr "One click"

msgid ""
"The map keeps every district and highlights {{highest}}, the value it set. "
"Every other view now shows {{highest}}, with no filter to set in each."
msgstr ""
"The map keeps every district and highlights {{highest}}, the value it set. "
"Every other view now shows {{highest}}, with no filter to set in each."

msgid "Look closer"
msgstr "Look closer"

msgid ""
"Right-click {{highest}} on the map, then Drill down into {{highest}}. Or "
"press Next, and the demo drills down for you."
msgstr ""
"Right-click {{highest}} on the map, then Drill down into {{highest}}. Or "
"press Next, and the demo drills down for you."

msgid "The whole district"
msgstr "The whole district"

msgid ""
"The map now shows {{highest}}'s {{count}} chiefdoms, on the classes it had "
"for the districts. Every one is in the top class, as {{highest}} is."
msgid_plural ""
"The map now shows {{highest}}'s {{count}} chiefdoms, on the classes it had "
"for the districts. Every one is in the top class, as {{highest}} is."
msgstr[0] ""
"The map now shows {{highest}}'s {{count}} chiefdoms, on the classes it had "
"for the districts. Every one is in the top class, as {{highest}} is."
msgstr[1] ""
"The map now shows {{highest}}'s {{count}} chiefdoms, on the classes it had "
"for the districts. Every one is in the top class, as {{highest}} is."

msgid "Not one hotspot"
msgstr "Not one hotspot"

msgid ""
"The chart now shows {{highest}}'s chiefdoms, month by month. Every one of "
"them stays above {{rate}}, the country's rate for the year, so the cause is "
"shared across the district."
msgstr ""
"The chart now shows {{highest}}'s chiefdoms, month by month. Every one of "
"them stays above {{rate}}, the country's rate for the year, so the cause is "
"shared across the district."

msgid "Why"
msgstr "Why"

msgid ""
"The table narrows to {{highest}}'s chiefdoms. In {{quarter}}, none of its "
"{{count}} reaches the {{target}}% target for the malaria vaccine, nor for "
"Penta 3, given at the same routine visits. Where malaria weighs most, "
"prevention reaches the fewest children. Pick Penta 3 in the data selector "
"after the tour, and the table shows it."
msgid_plural ""
"The table narrows to {{highest}}'s chiefdoms. In {{quarter}}, none of its "
"{{count}} reaches the {{target}}% target for the malaria vaccine, nor for "
"Penta 3, given at the same routine visits. Where malaria weighs most, "
"prevention reaches the fewest children. Pick Penta 3 in the data selector "
"after the tour, and the table shows it."
msgstr[0] ""
"The table narrows to {{highest}}'s chiefdoms. In {{quarter}}, none of its "
"{{count}} reaches the {{target}}% target for the malaria vaccine, nor for "
"Penta 3, given at the same routine visits. Where malaria weighs most, "
"prevention reaches the fewest children. Pick Penta 3 in the data selector "
"after the tour, and the table shows it."
msgstr[1] ""
"The table narrows to {{highest}}'s chiefdoms. In {{quarter}}, none of its "
"{{count}} reaches the {{target}}% target for the malaria vaccine, nor for "
"Penta 3, given at the same routine visits. Where malaria weighs most, "
"prevention reaches the fewest children. Pick Penta 3 in the data selector "
"after the tour, and the table shows it."

msgid "From where to why, in two clicks"
msgstr "From where to why, in two clicks"

msgid ""
"Without linked views, this takes three dashboards, the same filter set in "
"each, and care that they all show the same place and period. Here every "
"view stays on the same question. The other tour, How it works, shows how "
"the views are linked."
msgstr ""
"Without linked views, this takes three dashboards, the same filter set in "
"each, and care that they all show the same place and period. Here every "
"view stays on the same question. The other tour, How it works, shows how "
"the views are linked."

